{
 "version": 1,
 "_about": {
  "mount": "How the game hangs each weapon part on the hunter, read from the executable by C:\\MH3U-Extract\\mh3u_mount.py (notes/armor.md \"Weapon mount\"). A part's callback (cPlayerBase::WeaponCallback) places the part model's mount joint at the hunter bone `joint` (a bone id) times T(pos cm) R(rot degrees, ZYX) S(scale). `sheathed` and `drawn` are the part's placement with no special motion playing: the drawn flag picks state 1 (0 for the Dual Blades' second blade); shields are always held (state 4), the arrows and the Long Sword scabbard always rest (state 2). A rest state takes the class's rest scale (0.8 / 0.9 / 1.0).",
  "records": "The record tables are .bss filled at boot (static initialiser 0xa9f224), read by running it in an emulator (mh3u_static_init.py); the matrix convention was checked by running the callback's joint method 0x23bd14 on known inputs (mh3u_mount_probe.py).",
  "carry": "records[i] replaces a sheathed part's placement when the weapon's model has a carry index i (byModel, \"class:model\", the per-model table 0xbd0c24 row +6; the Dual Blades' second blade takes i + 1); not for the arrows (type 16) or the scabbard, whose record comes from elsewhere",
  "notRead": "Motion-specific placements (the per-type state functions switch on the motion id and its frame; the Light Bowgun and Switch Axe have keyframed tables for some motions); the alt table's game mode; the joint animation of a weapon's other joints (0x23aec8 per type)."
 },
 "order": "ZYX",
 "units": {
  "pos": "cm",
  "rot": "degrees"
 },
 "compose": "world(the part model's mountJoint) = world(hunter bone `joint`) * T(pos) * R(rot, ZYX) * S(scale)",
